# Dynamic text appearance

Nicknames and other user- or content-supplied strings go through `lib/ui/dynamic-text.ts` before they are rendered. Do not pick a one-off `maxLength`, ellipsis, or wrap at the call site.

## Length

- Nicknames: `clampNickname` (`NICKNAME_MAX_LENGTH`). Use that same constant as the input `maxLength`.
- Other dynamic copy (titles, captions): `clampDynamicText` with the budget for that surface.
- A loading scramble uses the clamped string’s length, not a magic character count. Scramble glyphs are wider than the settled letters; width math uses `dynamicTextWidthPx(..., scramble: true)`.

## Prefix + value

“dedicated by”, “in collaboration w/”, and any other fixed prefix beside a dynamic value:

- Fluid width: `AtomicLabeledText` with `measureKey` set to the clamped value. The prefix and the value are each `whitespace-nowrap`. If the scramble does not fit beside the prefix, the value moves to the next line as a whole and stays there after it reveals. Never let a scramble or a name break mid-glyph, and never slide a revealed name back onto the prefix line.
- Known pixel width (OG, canvas): `labeledValueStacks`. Stack when it returns true.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — inline name wraps one scramble glyph at a time
<p>{prefix} <EncryptedText text={name} /></p>

// ✅ GOOD
<AtomicLabeledText prefix={prefix} measureKey={clampNickname(name)}>
  <EncryptedText text={clampNickname(name)} />
</AtomicLabeledText>
```
